Third-party material
--------------------

custom_components/ps5/keys.py and the Remote Play parts of custom_components/ps5/protocol.py
  The key tables (HMAC key, registration key tables) are taken from pyremoteplay, and the
  wake-up, pairing and standby handshake is re-implemented after it, compared byte for byte
  against pyremoteplay 0.7.6.
  pyremoteplay: https://github.com/ktnrg45/pyremoteplay
  Copyright (c) ktnrg45, GNU General Public License v3.0
  pyremoteplay in turn derives these tables and the protocol from Chiaki
  (https://git.sr.ht/~thestr4ng3r/chiaki), an open source PlayStation Remote Play client.
  Because of this, the whole integration is licensed under the GPL v3.

custom_components/ps5/psn.py
  The PlayStation Network sign-in (NPSSO -> authorization code -> token) uses the same public
  client ID, redirect URI and scopes of the official PlayStation App that PSNAWP uses.
  No code is copied from PSNAWP.
  PSNAWP: https://github.com/isFakeAccount/psnawp
  Copyright (c) isFakeAccount, MIT License

